    rationale: `Factitious disorder imposed on another involves falsifying or inducing illness or injury in another person, such as a child, and presenting that person as ill, with deception evident even without obvious external rewards. DSM-5-TR gives the diagnosis to the perpetrator, while the victim may be given an abuse diagnosis or code. Because the behavior is a form of child maltreatment, a counselor who suspects it is also a mandated reporter.`,
